Moonaan patch of picomatch 4.0.7 for CVE-2026-112366 / GHSA-fc5q-39xc-vjpf.

picomatch is Copyright (c) 2017-present, Jon Schlinkert, released under the
MIT License (see LICENSE). This fork is unchanged from upstream tag 4.0.7 except:

- lib/parse.js + test/options.maxExtglobRecursion.js: upstream PR
  micromatch/picomatch#237 by Eduardo Seibt (head 1bf0d04563cb9ce568cf36efc5f6b7187d9911d5),
  which collapses single-branch repeated extglobs that contain a star
  (`+(P)` -> `(P)`, `*(P)` -> `(P)?`) so they no longer nest unbounded quantifiers.
- test/moonaan.cve-2026-112366.js: timing regression test.

Upstream PR #194 (named in the advisory) was evaluated and NOT used: it does not
bound `+(*)` / `+(*a)`.

Known residuals of this patch:
- Multi-branch repeated extglobs with a starred branch, e.g. `+(*a|*b)`,
  `+(*a|b)` or `*(*.js|*.ts)`, still backtrack exponentially (upstream #259
  closes these but literalizes slash-containing bodies such as `+(**/a)`).
- A bracket class that can match `/` inside the collapsed branch, e.g.
  `+(*[/])` or `+(*[[:punct:]])`, no longer matches multi-segment subjects
  such as `x//` (4.0.7 did).

Delete this fork once upstream releases a fixed version.
